# Prettier ignore list — see issue #1182.
#
# Format with: pnpm format      Check with: pnpm format:check
#
# Two directories are excluded, and the reasons are not interchangeable:

# 1. Agent skills are a size-capped document class, not prose.
#    AGENTS.md sets MAX_LINES_SKILL_MD=250, enforced by
#    scripts/validate-skill-format.sh. Prettier's markdown formatter is
#    net-line-positive on these files: it pads every table to the widest cell
#    and inserts a blank line around each list, which pushed
#    pr-review-fix/SKILL.md from 245 to 251 lines and broke the cap on a
#    formatting-only commit. A gate that punishes correct formatting is a
#    gate that gets disabled, so the two tools are kept disjoint: prettier
#    owns source and docs, the cap owns skills.
#    .pre-commit-config.yaml excludes the same paths, so the two stay in sync.
.agents/skills/
.opencode/skills/
.github/skills/

# 2. Third-party Impeccable skill files are vendored via a submodule/symlink.
#    Reformatting vendored content makes future upstream syncs conflict.
.impeccable/

# Generated output. Not source; a diff here is noise.
packages/ui/storybook-static/
packages/ui/coverage/
apps/web/dist/
apps/web/coverage/
apps/worker/dist/
coverage/

# Generated by pnpm, not by us. pnpm emits a blank line after `importers:`
# and keeps long `resolution: {integrity: sha512-…}` on one line, both of
# which prettier rewrites — so `format:check` failed every Dependabot PR
# (pnpm-lock.yaml was the only dirty file in runs for #1225–#1228) while the
# lockfile on main stayed clean because nothing had regenerated it in a form
# prettier disliked. Formatting a file we do not author is how two tools end
# up fighting: pnpm would rewrite prettier's version on the next install.
# ADR-288 (format ownership is partitioned) applied to the lockfile.
pnpm-lock.yaml
